1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,870
It had to be Mickey.

3
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,000
He's totally unreliable.

4
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:32,190
No wonder you're gonna be single forever.

5
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,110
Well, you've never managed to get married, either.

6
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,550
I'm trying to feel the wind.

7
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,470
He's nuts. Totally.

8
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,390
With a guy like you, it's no wonder...

9
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:40,830
No wonder what?

10
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,700
Right, Meatball!

11
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,060
A natural-born Yo-Yo prodigy.

12
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,500
What a waste.

13
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,870
So, loser trades Yo-Yos with the Winner.

14
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,000
Deal?

15
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,710
My Sky Raider is the newest model. No way.

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,500
Episode 3

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Hi,

18
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,260
You have to flick your wrist when you release it.

19
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:13,500
That's what gives it spin.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You...

21
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,220
Do you play Yo-Yo too?

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,500
Maybe.

23
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,100
Boss Zhang,

24
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:48,540
Come in.

25
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,740
Boss Zhang, I need your signature on this document.

26
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,950
Could you brew me some of that calming tea?

27
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:11,100
I'll have it after my meeting.

28
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,990
Sure, that way you'll be able to

29
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,460
sleep soundly on the plane.

30
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,580
Boss Zhang, if there's nothing else,
I'll take my leave now.

31
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,020
Okay, go ahead.

32
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,500
Hold on,

33
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,820
One of my Classmates is coming by to see me in a bit.

34
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,470
His name's Tony. When he gets here,
have him wait for me.

35
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,140
Got it.

36
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,580
You're from the Courier Company, right?

37
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,020
What took you so long?

38
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,900
Here you go. The address is written right here.

39
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:56,220
Miss, I'm not from a Courier Company.

40
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,140
Then who are you?

41
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:02,940
I'm here to see Boss Zhang. I'm his old Classmate.

42
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,820
Oh, you must be Mr. Tony.

43
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,260
Yes, that's me.

44
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:08,420
Boss Zhang mentioned you'd be coming.

45
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,660
He said to have you wait here for a bit.

46
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,060
He's in the middle of an important
video conference right now.

47
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:13,500
He can't step away just yet.

48
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,830
Oh, I see. Okay, no problem.

49
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:18,780
Sorry, I've got something to take care of right now.

50
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,180
There's water over there. Help yourself.

51
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,100
Alright, thanks.

52
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,180
That's an old Classmate for you.

53
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,580
He knew I was coming and already had tea brewed.

54
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,460
Looks like things are looking up today.

55
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,030
Old friend, for old times' sake...

56
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:15,420
Come on, what's a little bit of money between us?

57
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:16,380
Is it enough?

58
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,300
It's enough, really.

59
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,220
I've got more right here. I've got plenty of cash.

60
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,660
It's really enough. Enough, enough!

61
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,580
Really, it's plenty.

62
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,980
Boss Zhang! Boss Zhang! I've got enough, really.

63
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:27,900
Old buddy, hey pal.

64
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:29,820
No, no more.

65
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,700
I'm good, Boss Zhang. Seriously, it's enough.

66
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:37,020
I don't want it! I really don't need any more! I'm good!

67
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,460
Tony!

68
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,830
I said no more! No more!

69
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:41,770
What's going on?

70
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Tony?

71
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,660
No more! We agreed on the phone!

72
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,420
I've got a plane to catch. I'm out of time.

73
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,250
Secretary Li,

74
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,780
When he wakes up, if he needs anything, just let me know.

75
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,180
Assistant Wang, let's go.

76
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:01,500
Boss Zhang, take care.

77
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,740
Secretary Li, phone call.

78
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,500
Coming!

79
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,180
Ready... go!

80
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,200
Oh no!

81
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,470
Haha, I win!

82
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:51,900
Hand over your Sky Raider.

83
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,180
Haha! A Super Nuclear Fission!

84
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,620
You got played, kid.

85
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,540
That's just a regular Nuclear Fission.

86
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:01,980
It's been around forever.

87
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,380
It's a fake. Give it back.

88
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:09,180
Maybe... we should just give it back to him.

89
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:13,500
Why should we? He agreed to the terms himself.

90
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:14,940
You win some, you lose some.

91
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:16,830
Tell you what.

92
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,750
I'll have a match with you on this kid's behalf.

93
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,220
Same rules as before. Deal?

94
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,620
Well, if you're so eager to help,

95
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:25,020
you've gotta put something on the line, right?

96
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:26,460
Fine.

97
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,900
If I lose,

98
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,300
you can have this Fire Warrior of mine.

99
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:32,220
Alright, that's fair.

100
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,900
Hey, kid. You trust me, right?

101
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:35,700
I trust you.

102
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:43,260
Don't worry, he's just a rookie.

103
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,180
Chuck, go!

104
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,430
Now what do we do?

105
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,900
We can't just let him sleep here at the office.

106
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,400
Sis, look! They're having a match over there.

107
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:11,620
Looks like Chuck and the others.

108
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:14,500
It's him!

109
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,220
Then let me show you a few moves I've got.

110
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,620
Just a little teaser.

111
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:32,220
And now for my second trick: "Breakaway!"

112
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,780
And now for my third trick:

113
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,220
"Scaling the Summit!"

114
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:51,420
How's that?

115
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,180
Not bad. Now check this out!

116
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:10,620
"Baby's Cradle."

117
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,260
Pretty good, right?

118
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,500
Awesome!

119
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,020
He can even do the "Crazy Cradle"

120
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,380
Looks like I'll have to bust out my secret weapon.

121
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,340
Watch this.

122
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,780
"Magic Gloves."

123
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,180
Hang on a sec.

124
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:29,820
Hand it over.

125
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:51,420
What's wrong?

126
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,300
He's too good. I can't beat him.

127
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,180
Hey, where are you from?

128
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:01,390
Does it matter?

129
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:04,860
Yay!

130
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:08,960
Have it back.

131
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:10,140
Thanks, big bro!

132
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,100
Now get on home.

133
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:12,540
Let's go!

134
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,300
This is ridiculous!

135
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,900
What a show-off.

136
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,900
The second you mention money,

137
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,780
even an old buddy who used
to sleep in the bunk above you

138
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,180
turns on you.

139
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,460
But some things...

140
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,340
money or no money,

141
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:21,180
you've just got to make them happen.

142
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,380
Lady Luck.

143
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,220
Today, I'm destined for a beautiful encounter.

144
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,380
I heard Coach Tony put Mark
in charge of selecting the Team.

145
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,780
What? So he doesn't have to go through tryouts?

146
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:10,140
Of course not! Mark's already a Top-Tier Player.

147
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,580
At our District Tournament last year,

148
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,500
He got first place!

149
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,900
First place!

150
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,740
Sis, hurry up! It's about to start!

151
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:38,940
Mark's here!

152
00:13:39,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Mark! Mark!

153
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,900
Excuse me, can you tell me
where Jianghai High School is?

154
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,300
Oh, okay. Thanks.

155
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:08,500
Ah! What a cute guy!

156
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,100
Where? Where is he?

157
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,020
Hmph. He's long gone.

158
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,700
The tryouts are about to begin.

159
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:25,500
Before we get started,
I have an Announcement to make.

160
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,820
I'm officially appointing Mark

161
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:33,660
as the Captain of our Jianghai Team.

162
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:36,060
Oh, so they've already decided
Mark's gonna be the Captain.

163
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,500
Yeah!

164
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,350
I heard Mark is really something else.

165
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,340
He's unbeaten in the whole School.

166
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,260
Well, of course. He was the District Champion last year.

167
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,140
Having a Captain this good is awesome!

168
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,420
Alright, settle down. Settle down!

169
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:54,300
Today's tryouts

170
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:58,140
will be co-hosted by Mark and myself.

171
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:00,540
We have full authority to decide.

172
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,340
Everyone gets a fair shot! Equal opportunity!
The best players make the Team!

173
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:09,180
Alright, everyone will take the stage
in the order listed on the sign-up sheet.

174
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,620
One by one.

175
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,000
Ah!

176
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:19,740
Matthew

177
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,860
Do you need me to take you to the hospital?

178
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,270
No, it's fine.

179
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,220
There's a clinic at school. Just take me there.

180
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,630
Which school do you go to?

181
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,140
Jianghai High School.

182
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:35,500
Really!

183
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,750
Wait, Mini?

184
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,180
Wait, it's already started?

185
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,620
I'll be right there!

186
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,060
Your foot...

187
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,500
Don't worry about it. Thanks for the ride!

188
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,260
Matthew passes!

189
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:10,500
Next!

190
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:15,900
Nice.

191
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:26,940
Alright, next!

192
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:31,500
Next, next!

193
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:38,900
Next!

194
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,460
Next up, Mini!

195
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,860
Go, Sis! You got this!

196
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,180
Wait, wait, wait!

197
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,500
This is killing me! Let me go first!

198
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:15,900
Mark, I'm up first!

199
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,580
I need dark clouds!

200
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,180
Good, good, good!

201
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,180
Okay, you pass.

202
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:54,780
How come she just walked off without finishing?

203
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,940
Hmph. That guy was acting all
shady in front of my sister.

204
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,500
Something's up.

205
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:01,500
Next!

206
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:05,340
Shawn?

207
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,500
Leo, summer break is about to start at school.

208
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,860
The School decided to assign you
to a class next Semester.

209
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,300
But

210
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,140
we welcome you to study here
at your Father's old alma mater.

211
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:25,020
Thanks. Can I maybe take a look around?

212
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:25,980
Of course.

213
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,220
Judges.

214
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:51,900
It's coming.

215
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,740
Just go home and sleep.

216
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,580
You don't even know who he is?

217
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,940
He's our School's famous Yo-Yo Theory Expert!

218
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:05,340
They call him "The Squirrel."

219
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,260
Some expert.

220
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:09,180
He can't even pull off "Around the World."

221
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,070
And he wants to make the Team?

222
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:13,470
Coach!

223
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:14,430
Coach!

224
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,420
Coach!

225
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,180
Huh? What is it?

226
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,020
Him again?

227
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:26,460
How many times is this?

228
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:28,860
That's the 18th time, Coach.

229
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:35,100
18 times!

230
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:37,500
What about Mark? Why isn't he stopping this?

231
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:39,900
Mark took off a long time ago.

232
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,620
Shawn...

233
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:49,980
Get off the stage!

234
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:51,900
Shawn!

235
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:56,220
Time for a break.

236
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:00,060
No, no! I'm not tired! Really, I'm fine!

237
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:02,200
I'm tired.

238
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:05,820
Stop right now!

239
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:10,140
Hold on! Coach Tony, I still
haven't shown you my Signature Move!

240
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,580
That secret move is me,

241
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,980
Shawn, future Yo-Yo Master!

242
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,310
It's a variation I created based
on "Crescent Moon Loop."

243
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,780
I call it "Steal the Sky and Swap the Sun!"

244
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:25,500
Thanks.

245
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,900
Of course, this move

246
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,820
absolutely requires dark clouds.

247
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:33,180
Everyone, please be patient.

248
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:37,500
Get off! Get off the stage! Off!

249
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:49,800
Dark clouds!

250
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:54,780
The heavens are on my side!

251
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,620
And now, everyone, behold my self-created secret move:

252
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,540
"Steal the Sky and Swap the Sun!"

253
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,300
What kind of move is that?

254
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:07,740
I've never seen it before.

255
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:11,070
But he can't even do the basics!

256
00:21:17,020 --> 00:21:17,820
Hey! What are you waiting for?

257
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:19,500
Behold!

